# Proposed features recognized from block_level.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F2: the level at z=20.0, below the part's topmost height and with nothing beside it rising above it: 1 face (F2) at one height; nothing stands above it outside a proposed feature, so the whole blank clears to it around what stands, the islands and voids derived from containment (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F2_Floor, stepover=...)  [the whole blank down to z=20.0, around what stands higher]
# then finish with: run End(tool=..., surface=F2_Floor, stepover=...)
# what stands higher is an island by containment, and a pocket or bore that opens in this floor is
# cut from it by its own run
feature F2_Floor Plane(z=20.0)

# F4: through-trim wall loop F6 F8 F14 F4 on part-bottom anchor F17: straight top edges form a closed 3D wire (z 12.0..20.0), walls descend to the part bottom at z=0.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.8)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F4_Trim)  [an Endmill -- the wall is a flank cut; the wire carries its own Z range]
# extent=20.0 reaches the part bottom below the wire's highest point; where the wire dips,
# the pass rides below the bottom -- a through trim, nothing below to cut
# the wire's XY projection is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention, DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# every segment is a straight line (a curved trim edge refuses instead of tessellating), so the
# comp=control rule for recognized contours does not bind -- either comp mode is legal
feature F4_Trim ContourBoss(extent=20.0
    0.0 0.0 12.0
    0.0 40.0 12.0
    8.0 40.0 20.0
    60.0 40.0 20.0
    60.0 0.0 20.0
    8.0 0.0 20.0
)

# F9: pocket floor at z=14.0; vertical wall loop F12 F5 F18 F24 F23, mouth at z=20.0, depth 6.0, opens upward; 1 inner wire -- standing material inside the pocket proposes beside it; the floor runs out onto F1, which falls away from it -- that side is open, the loop drawn straight out past the blank; floor fillet R1.0 (F10 F7 F19 F21 F20) -- the loop is drawn at the walls, the sharp corner; mouth rounded R1.0 (F3 F11 F13 F15 F16) -- proposed as edge_round, the mouth at the round's top (CHECKLIST row 2.7)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F9_Pocket, stepover=...)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# or finish with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F9_Pocket, comp=control)
# comp=control is required on recognized profile Side runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# this floor has 1 inner wire: a boss proposed INSIDE this loop is its island, derived from
# containment -- the Clear above goes around it (stepover at most the tool's radius), and the
# island takes no Clear of its own. CHECK that every inner wire has a proposed boss below:
# standing material this reader could not name is NOT in the proposal, and would be cleared through.
# open toward F1: the floor runs out onto a face that falls away, so
# that side is drawn straight out past the blank, where the engine reads it open;
# everything the loop holds past the floor is air in the model above this floor
# the model has a floor fillet R1.0: the loop is the walls' own line, so a flat
# endmill cuts the corner square, past the model; an endmill with that corner
# radius leaves the fillet
# break the mouth with: run Form(tool=<CornerRounder>, surface=F9_Pocket)  [its ground arc must be R1.0]
feature F9_Pocket ProfilePocket(z=20.0, extent=6.0, edge_round=1.0
    -0.02 8.0
    40.0 8.0
    40.603 8.036
    41.197 8.145
    41.773 8.325
    42.324 8.573
    42.84 8.885
    43.316 9.257
    43.743 9.684
    44.115 10.16
    44.427 10.676
    44.675 11.227
    44.855 11.803
    44.964 12.397
    45.0 13.0
    45.0 27.0
    44.964 27.603
    44.855 28.197
    44.675 28.773
    44.427 29.324
    44.115 29.84
    43.743 30.316
    43.316 30.743
    42.84 31.115
    42.324 31.427
    41.773 31.675
    41.197 31.855
    40.603 31.964
    40.0 32.0
    -0.02 32.0
)

# F22: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material inside (a standing boss), flat top cap F25, clean base at z=14.0 (CHECKLIST row 2.4)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F22_Boss, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# the tool rides outside at R + r_tool (convex flank; finish_cylinder's mirror)
feature F22_Boss CylinderBoss(dia=10.0, extent=12.0, x=28.0, y=20.0, z=14.0)

# F25: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F25_Top Plane(z=26.0)
